    "innovation": "This paper introduces a novel method for producing finer wool threads by stretching thicker yarns, a technique proposed by Mr. H. J. W. Bliss to potentially create lightweight fabrics from comparatively coarse wool.",
    "kg_extraction_triplets": [
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "westerly component of sea-ice motion",
            "source_entity_type": "Ocean_Circulation",
            "relation": "OBSERVED_IN_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Antarctica",
            "target_entity_type": "Continent",
            "paragraph": "One important point which has been learned from the drifts of ships such as the Belgica, the Gauss, the Endurance, and the Aurora, which have been beset and carried with the ice, is that there is a considerable westerly component in its motion. The chief motive power of the drift is undoubtedly the wind flowing down from the continental ice-sheet, which is generally south-easterly in direction, and so accounts for some of the westerly component.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "westerly component of sea-ice motion",
            "source_entity_type": "Ocean_Circulation",
            "relation": "OBSERVED_IN_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Weddell Sea",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "But for the navigator it is very important to keep in mind the general westerly tendency. For example, attempts to get south in the Weddell Sea are much more likely to succeed along the east coast than along the west.",
